<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_ScarlandsMark.xml                UtinniPatches - SCARLANDS_MECHANICS_2 build pass

  scarlands_kit_spec.md §2 (the Scarlands mark). Owner ruling 4 (card sitting
  2026-09-11): "both — a small permanent mood hit AND nightmares while on
  Scarlands maps; leaving the map ends the nightmares, never the mark."

  Application: RUT_ScarlandsMarkLock.xml (GameConditionDefs/) grants this
  hediff via EnvironmentalWeatherExtension.hediffToApply/
  hediffSeverityPerInterval — RESOLVED zero-C# by the spike pass (both
  fields already shipped on RC4 by MIASMA_MECHANICS_1's M4 build). Severity
  math below is this pass's own INVENTED-BUILD split of the spec's own
  INVENTED "+0.2/day on-map; -0.1/day off-map; floor 0.25 once severity ever
  exceeded 0.5" into two independent, already-shipped comps rather than one
  new one:

    - HediffCompProperties_SeverityPerDay (vanilla): severityPerDay -0.1,
      running unconditionally (both on- and off-map) — the constant fade
      half.
    - RUT_ScarlandsMarkLock's own hediffSeverityPerInterval: +0.3/day GROSS
      while the permanent condition is active (damageIntervalTicks 2500,
      ~24 applications/day -> 0.3/24 = 0.0125/application), netting against
      the -0.1/day comp above to +0.2/day NET while on a Scarlands map —
      matching the spec's own on-map figure exactly. Off-map the
      GameCondition is not running (it is a per-map permanent condition),
      so only the -0.1/day comp acts, matching the spec's own off-map
      figure exactly.
    - HediffCompProperties_SeverityFloor (RM_HediffComp_SeverityFloor, this
      spike's own new C#): floorTriggerThreshold 0.5, floorValue 0.25 —
      the spec's own numbers, verbatim. Deliberately equals this hediff's
      own "mild exposure" stage threshold below, so a floored pawn settles
      permanently at "the mark, faded to its floor" rather than oscillating
      across a stage boundary.

  Stages/mood/nightmares: vanilla ThoughtWorker_Hediff (RUT_ScarlandsMarkThoughts.xml,
  ThoughtDefs/) index-aligns its own <stages> list to THIS hediff's stage
  index (ThoughtWorker_Hediff.CurrentStateInternal, decompile-confirmed) —
  the two files' stage counts and thresholds must move together. Nightmares
  are vanilla HediffStage.mentalStateGivers (Hediff.cs:463, decompile-
  confirmed this spike pass) on the top two stages, per the spec's own
  "nightmares from 0.5 up."

  MayRequire is load-bearing: the compClass (RM_HediffComp_SeverityFloor)
  lives in mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards; per memory
  (modextension-missing-type-discards-def) an unresolvable comp class risks
  discarding the whole def silently.

  STAGED-LORE COUPLING (kit spec's own note): description below is §P
  register only (no §GM truth) — deepens later via STAGED_LORE_BUILD_1's
  live def-description swaps, not built here.
-->
<Defs>

  <HediffDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_ScarlandsMark</defName>
    <label>the Scarlands mark</label>
    <description>Something about this place gets under the skin and stays there — bad dreams, a shadow on the mood, a weight that never quite lifts even long after the dust of the Scarlands is washed off. The Jawa have a word for it. They are right.</description>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <defaultLabelColor>(0.55,0.2,0.25)</defaultLabelColor>
    <minSeverity>0.0001</minSeverity>
    <initialSeverity>0.0001</initialSeverity>
    <makesSickThought>false</makesSickThought>
    <tendable>false</tendable>
    <maxSeverity>1.0</maxSeverity>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>onset</label>
        <becomeVisible>false</becomeVisible>
      </li>
      <li>
        <minSeverity>0.25</minSeverity>
        <label>mild mark</label>
      </li>
      <li>
        <minSeverity>0.5</minSeverity>
        <label>deepening mark</label>
        <mentalStateGivers>
          <li>
            <mentalState>Wander_Sad</mentalState>
            <mtbDays>6</mtbDays>
          </li>
        </mentalStateGivers>
      </li>
      <li>
        <minSeverity>0.75</minSeverity>
        <label>heavy mark</label>
        <mentalStateGivers>
          <li>
            <mentalState>Wander_Sad</mentalState>
            <mtbDays>3</mtbDays>
          </li>
        </mentalStateGivers>
      </li>
    </stages>
    <comps>
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_SeverityPerDay">
        <severityPerDay>-0.1</severityPerDay>
      </li>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.HediffCompProperties_SeverityFloor">
        <floorTriggerThreshold>0.5</floorTriggerThreshold>
        <floorValue>0.25</floorValue>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </HediffDef>

</Defs>
